IMPORT prelude

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (Western Australia) -- who is a worker and who is the employer (s 12, s 13,
-- s 215); the employer's liability (ss 6, 17, 19, 20); income compensation (ss 46, 48, 51, 55-57); medical and health expenses
-- (ss 69, 75-78); lump sum permanent impairment compensation (ss 97, 100, 101, selected Table items); who assesses permanent
-- impairment (s 186); compulsory insurance (ss 202, 204); and the common law: the 15% threshold for damages against the employer
-- (ss 415, 416, 421, 422), the effect of an election under 25% (s 423), the cap under 25% (s 424), and third parties (s 434).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 48940, Act No. 21 of 2023, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48940.txt. The deposit names no compilation or reprint number. Its compilation table ends
-- with the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Amendment (Common Law Election Validation) Act 2024 (No. 40 of 2024; in
-- operation 30 October 2024). The Act other than a few early provisions came into operation on 1 July 2024.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0011 (priority 1), raised 4 times by the Western Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios:
-- Jake k044 (2029-04-12, a delivery rider on an ABN hit by a car door; "Who pays for a contractor hurt by a car?"; the scenario
-- cites "s 5 (worker: not an independent contractor on these facts)"), Jake k085 (2053-10-05, a fall on a wet stairwell on
-- patrol for Sentinel in Jarrah's tower; eleven weeks off; a whole person impairment assessed at 14%; "What is paid; who assesses
-- impairment; what does 15% unlock?"), Daniel d044 (2031-06-01, Jarrah's first three employees; "Part 8 (compulsory insurance)")
-- and Daniel d080 (2053-10-05, the same fall seen from the tenant's side; "Part 2 (the employer's liability lies with Sentinel)").
-- SCOPED to those questions, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them. The scenarios' Part numbers
-- are not this Act's: here s 5 only points to s 12 for "worker"; permanent impairment assessment is Part 4; insurance is Part 5
-- (Part 8 is Administration); the common law is Part 7. The provisions that answer the questions are encoded wherever they sit.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: journeys (s 9), diseases (ss 10, 11, Part 2 Division 9), labour hire (s 14), jockeys (s 15), working directors
-- (s 16), claims procedure and provisional payments (Part 2 Division 2), the pre-injury weekly rate calculation itself (s 54; an
-- INPUT), the s 57(3) minimum weekly rate calculation (an INPUT), additional income compensation (s 52), miscellaneous and
-- rehabilitation expenses (Divisions 5, 6), noise-induced hearing loss, death, settlement (Division 12), injury management
-- (Part 3), dispute resolution (Part 6), double recovery (Part 7 Division 3), choice of law, and everything from Part 8 on except
-- s 538(1). Amounts set by regulations -- the maximum weekly rate of income compensation (s 53), the maximum damages amount for
-- less than 25% impairment (s 424), any greater percentage under s 69 -- are INPUTS. The general maximum amount is stated in
-- s 538(1) as $243 991 but "may be updated" and varied by regulations (s 538(3)); it is an INPUT, and the cases use $243 991.
-- Whether an individual's work is part of a trade or business he regularly carries on in his own name (s 12(2)(c)(i)) is a
-- question of fact; it is an INPUT.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (WA) -- compensation`

§§ `helpers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `12, 13 -- worker`

-- s 12(2): "An individual is a worker if -- (a) the individual has entered into, or works under, a contract of service with a
-- person ...; or (b) [an apprentice under a contract and a registered training contract]; or (c) the individual has contracted
-- with a person for the performance of work by the individual and -- (i) the work is not work in the course of or incidental to
-- a trade or business regularly carried on by the individual in the individual's own name or under a business or firm name; and
-- (ii) the individual does not sublet the contract; and (iii) if the individual employs a worker, the individual performs part
-- of the work personally."
-- s 12(3): "The person with whom the worker has entered into the contract, or for whom the worker works under the contract, is
-- the worker's employer."
-- s 13(1): regulations may provide that an individual of a specified class "who otherwise would not be, or might not be, a worker"
-- is a worker; s 13(3): regulations may provide that one who otherwise would be "is not a worker". No regulations were retrieved;
-- both are INPUTS.
DECLARE Engagement HAS
    `a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an apprenticeship under a registered training contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contract for the performance of work by him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is in the course of a trade or business he regularly carries on in his own name or a business name` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he sublets the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he employs a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he performs part of the work personally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulations under s 13(1) make him a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulations under s 13(3) exclude him` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the engagement` IS AN Engagement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `he is a contractor-worker under s 12(2)(c)` IF
        `the engagement`'s `a contract for the performance of work by him`
    AND (NOT `the engagement`'s `the work is in the course of a trade or business he regularly carries on in his own name or a business name`)
    AND (NOT `the engagement`'s `he sublets the contract`)
    AND (    (NOT `the engagement`'s `he employs a worker`)
         OR  `the engagement`'s `he performs part of the work personally`)

GIVEN `the engagement` IS AN Engagement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `he is a worker` IF
        (NOT `the engagement`'s `regulations under s 13(3) exclude him`)
    AND (    `the engagement`'s `a contract of service`
         OR  `the engagement`'s `an apprenticeship under a registered training contract`
         OR  `he is a contractor-worker under s 12(2)(c)` `the engagement`
         OR  `the engagement`'s `regulations under s 13(1) make him a worker`)

-- s 12(3): only the other party to the worker's contract is the employer. A person with no contract with him (a tenant of the
-- building where he works, a driver on the road) is not his employer under s 12.
GIVEN `the engagement` IS AN Engagement, `the person is the other party to his contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is his employer under s 12(3)` IF
        `he is a worker` `the engagement`
    AND `the person is the other party to his contract`

§§ `215 -- principal and contractor both taken to be employers`

-- s 215(1): if a worker suffers an injury from employment with a contractor that is relevant employment, "both the principal and
-- the contractor are, for the purposes of this Act, taken to be employers of the worker" and are "jointly and severally liable".
-- s 215(2): relevant employment if "(a) the employment is in performance of any work by or under the contractor; and (b) the work
-- on which the worker is employed is directly a part of or process in the trade or business of the principal; and (c) the injury
-- arises in respect of premises on which the principal has undertaken to do the work or that are otherwise under the control or
-- management of the principal." s 214: a principal is "a person who contracts with a contractor for the execution of any work".
-- s 220: the Subdivision does not make either liable "to pay any damages" they would not otherwise pay.
GIVEN `the person contracted with his employer for the work` IS A BOOLEAN, `he was employed in performing that work` IS A BOOLEAN, `the work is directly part of the person's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN, `the premises are the person's or under the person's control or management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is also taken to be his employer as principal` IF
        `the person contracted with his employer for the work`
    AND `he was employed in performing that work`
    AND `the work is directly part of the person's trade or business`
    AND `the premises are the person's or under the person's control or management`

§§ `6, 17, 19, 20 -- the employer's liability`

-- s 6(2): "A personal injury by accident is an injury from employment if the injury arises out of or in the course of the
-- employment or while the worker is acting under the employer's instructions."
-- s 17(1): "An employer is liable for compensation if a worker suffers an injury from employment with the employer."
-- s 19(1): "Liability for compensation arises only if the worker's employment is connected with this State."
-- s 20(2): no liability if it is "proved before an arbitrator" that the injury is attributable to impairing alcohol or drugs,
-- failure to use protective equipment provided, or "other serious and wilful misconduct"; s 20(3): this "does not exclude
-- liability if the worker's injury has serious and permanent effects on the worker or results in the death of the worker".
-- (s 20(4), a reasonable excuse for not using protective equipment, is folded into the misconduct input.)
GIVEN `arises out of or in the course of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `while acting under the employer's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the personal injury by accident is an injury from employment` IF
    `arises out of or in the course of the employment` OR `while acting under the employer's instructions`

GIVEN `the engagement` IS AN Engagement, `injury from employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `employment connected with this State` IS A BOOLEAN, `section 20 misconduct proved before an arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious and permanent effects or death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is liable for compensation` IF
        `he is a worker` `the engagement`
    AND `injury from employment`
    AND `employment connected with this State`
    AND (    (NOT `section 20 misconduct proved before an arbitrator`)
         OR  `serious and permanent effects or death`)

§§ `46, 48, 51, 55, 56, 57 -- income compensation`

-- s 55(2): for "the first 26 weeks in which income compensation is payable", total incapacity is paid "at the worker's preinjury
-- weekly rate of income"; s 55(3): after that, "at 85% of the worker's preinjury weekly rate of income", in each case "except as
-- otherwise provided in section 56 or 57". s 55(4)(b): a week counts if compensation "is payable for any day or days during the
-- week".
-- s 56: a payment above "the maximum weekly rate of income compensation" (prescribed by the regulations, s 53: an INPUT) "must be
-- reduced" to it.
-- s 57(2): a payment below the minimum weekly rate in s 57(3) is "to be increased" to it (the minimum is an INPUT; pass 0 where
-- s 57(7) says no minimum applies).
-- The s 55(5) indexation of the base rate of pay is not modelled; the pre-injury weekly rate passed in is the one that applies.
GIVEN `preinjury weekly rate` IS A NUMBER, `week number` IS A NUMBER, `maximum weekly rate` IS A NUMBER, `minimum weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`weekly income compensation for total incapacity` MEANS
    IF `s 55 amount` GREATER THAN `maximum weekly rate`
    THEN `maximum weekly rate`
    ELSE IF `s 55 amount` LESS THAN `minimum weekly rate`
         THEN `minimum weekly rate`
         ELSE `s 55 amount`
    WHERE
        `s 55 amount` MEANS
            IF `week number` AT MOST 26
            THEN `preinjury weekly rate`
            ELSE `preinjury weekly rate` TIMES 85 DIVIDED BY 100

-- The total for an unbroken run of weeks of total incapacity counted from the first week: the weeks within the first 26 at the
-- full rate, the rest at 85%, each capped at the maximum. (No minimum: the cases use rates above any minimum.)
GIVEN `preinjury weekly rate` IS A NUMBER, `weeks` IS A NUMBER, `maximum weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`income compensation for the first weeks of total incapacity` MEANS
        (`the smaller of` `weeks` 26 TIMES `weekly income compensation for total incapacity` `preinjury weekly rate` 1 `maximum weekly rate` 0)
    PLUS (`the larger of` (`weeks` MINUS 26) 0 TIMES `weekly income compensation for total incapacity` `preinjury weekly rate` 27 `maximum weekly rate` 0)

-- s 48(2): for partial incapacity, the total-incapacity amount less "the amount the worker earns, or is able to earn, in
-- suitable employment"; s 48(3): nothing if that equals or exceeds the total-incapacity amount.
GIVEN `total incapacity amount` IS A NUMBER, `able to earn in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`weekly income compensation for partial incapacity` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`total incapacity amount` MINUS `able to earn in suitable employment`) 0

-- s 51(1): entitlement "ceases when the total of all amounts of income compensation paid to the worker for that incapacity reaches
-- the income compensation general limit amount", which s 45 makes "equal to the general maximum amount" (s 538(1): $243 991,
-- adjustable by regulations; an INPUT).
GIVEN `income compensation paid so far` IS A NUMBER, `general maximum amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entitlement to income compensation has ceased` IF
    `income compensation paid so far` AT LEAST `general maximum amount`

§§ `69, 75, 76, 77, 78 -- medical and health expenses`

-- s 69: "medical and health expenses general limit amount means the amount that is 60%, or a greater percentage, if any,
-- prescribed by the regulations, of the general maximum amount"; "standard increase limit amount" is "40% ... of the medical and
-- health expenses general limit amount"; "special increase limit amount" is "190% ... of" it (in each case "or a greater
-- percentage, if any, prescribed by the regulations"; pass 0 for none).
-- s 75: the total "must not exceed the medical and health expenses general limit amount".
GIVEN `general maximum amount` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the medical and health expenses general limit amount` MEANS
    `general maximum amount` TIMES (`the larger of` 60 `prescribed percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `medical general limit` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard increase limit amount` MEANS
    `medical general limit` TIMES (`the larger of` 40 `prescribed percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `medical general limit` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special increase limit amount` MEANS
    `medical general limit` TIMES (`the larger of` 190 `prescribed percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 76: "When the total amount of medical and health expenses compensation paid ... reaches 60% of the medical and health expenses
-- general limit amount", the employer or insurer "must within 14 days give the worker notice of that fact".
GIVEN `medical compensation paid` IS A NUMBER, `medical general limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker must be given the 60% notice` IF
    `medical compensation paid` AT LEAST `medical general limit` TIMES 60 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 78(2), (3), (6): a special increase needs a prior standard increase, special expenses beyond what a standard increase can
-- provide, "a degree of permanent whole of person impairment of at least 15%" (s 79), the arbitrator's satisfaction as to the
-- regulations and the worker's needs, and an application within 5 years of the determination of liability.
GIVEN `a standard increase has been ordered` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER, `special expenses exceed a standard increase` IS A BOOLEAN, `the arbitrator is otherwise satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied within 5 years of the determination of liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arbitrator may order a special increase` IF
        `a standard increase has been ordered`
    AND `whole person impairment` AT LEAST 15
    AND `special expenses exceed a standard increase`
    AND `the arbitrator is otherwise satisfied`
    AND `applied within 5 years of the determination of liability`

§§ `97, 100, 101 -- lump sum compensation for permanent impairment`

-- s 97(1): payable "as a lump sum amount for permanent impairment suffered by a worker as a result of an injury that is personal
-- injury by accident"; s 97(2): "only for permanent impairment of a kind described in column 1 of the Table to section 101";
-- s 97(3): "payable only when the employer's liability to the worker for compensation for the injury is commuted by a settlement
-- agreement registered under Division 12".
-- s 101(1)(b): for less than 100%, "the amount calculated by multiplying the percentage degree of permanent impairment by the
-- percentage of the lump sum limit that is indicated for the impairment in column 2 of the Table"; s 100(1) and s 101(2): the
-- lump sum limit is the general maximum amount "applying on the day on which the injury occurred".
-- The degree is of the part or faculty of the body (s 98(2)(a)), not the whole person, except for scarring (s 98(2)(b)).
-- Only some of the 45 Table items are encoded (column 2 percentage in brackets).
DECLARE TableItem IS ONE OF
    `impairment of the back (thoracic spine or lumbar spine or both)`
    `impairment of the neck (including cervical spine)`
    `impairment of the pelvis`
    `impairment of arm at or above elbow`
    `impairment of arm below elbow`
    `impairment of hand or thumb and 4 fingers`
    `impairment of thumb`
    `impairment of leg at or above knee`
    `impairment of leg below knee`
    `impairment of foot`
    `impairment from facial scarring or disfigurement`
    `impairment from bodily, other than facial, scarring or disfigurement`

GIVEN `the item` IS A TableItem
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `impairment of the back (thoracic spine or lumbar spine or both)` THEN 75
    WHEN `impairment of the neck (including cervical spine)` THEN 55
    WHEN `impairment of the pelvis` THEN 30
    WHEN `impairment of arm at or above elbow` THEN 90
    WHEN `impairment of arm below elbow` THEN 80
    WHEN `impairment of hand or thumb and 4 fingers` THEN 80
    WHEN `impairment of thumb` THEN 35
    WHEN `impairment of leg at or above knee` THEN 70
    WHEN `impairment of leg below knee` THEN 65
    WHEN `impairment of foot` THEN 65
    WHEN `impairment from facial scarring or disfigurement` THEN 80
    WHEN `impairment from bodily, other than facial, scarring or disfigurement` THEN 50

GIVEN `the item` IS A TableItem, `degree of permanent impairment` IS A NUMBER, `general maximum amount on the day of injury` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`permanent impairment compensation` MEANS
    `general maximum amount on the day of injury` TIMES `the Table percentage` `the item` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `degree of permanent impairment` DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 100(2): with more than one impairment from an injury, the limit "applies as a limit on the aggregate".
GIVEN `sum of the separate amounts` IS A NUMBER, `general maximum amount on the day of injury` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total permanent impairment compensation` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `sum of the separate amounts` `general maximum amount on the day of injury`

GIVEN `personal injury by accident` IS A BOOLEAN, `liability commuted by a registered settlement agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `an election under s 421 registered with whole person impairment under 25%` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent impairment compensation is payable` IF
        `personal injury by accident`
    AND `liability commuted by a registered settlement agreement`
    AND (NOT `an election under s 421 registered with whole person impairment under 25%`)

§§ `183, 186 -- who assesses permanent impairment`

-- s 186(1): "The assessment of a worker's degree of permanent impairment must be made by an approved permanent impairment assessor
-- except as provided by subsection (2)"; s 186(2): for a dust disease, "by a Dust Disease Medical Panel". s 193(1): WorkCover WA
-- "may approve a medical practitioner as a permanent impairment assessor". s 183: assessed under the Permanent Impairment
-- Guidelines, "as a percentage".
DECLARE Assessor IS ONE OF
    `an approved permanent impairment assessor`
    `a Dust Disease Medical Panel`
    `the worker's treating medical practitioner, not approved`
    `the insurer's medical adviser, not approved`

GIVEN `the assessor` IS AN Assessor, `a dust disease` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assessment is one Part 4 allows` IF
    CONSIDER `the assessor`
    WHEN `an approved permanent impairment assessor` THEN NOT `a dust disease`
    WHEN `a Dust Disease Medical Panel` THEN `a dust disease`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `202, 204 -- compulsory insurance`

-- s 202(2): "An employer must at all times have a current workers compensation policy issued by a licensed insurer." s 202(3): not
-- "while the employer is a selfinsurer". There is no minimum number of workers or payroll.
-- s 204(1): failure is an offence; "Penalty for this subsection: a fine of $10 000 in respect of each of the employer's workers to
-- whom the offence relates."
GIVEN `number of workers` IS A NUMBER, `a selfinsurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must hold a current workers compensation policy` IF
        `number of workers` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `a selfinsurer`)

GIVEN `number of workers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for being uninsured` MEANS
    10000 TIMES `number of workers`

§§ `411, 415, 416, 421, 422, 434 -- the common law`

-- s 411: "third party means a person other than the employer". s 412: "employer" includes a person for whose acts the employer is
-- vicariously liable.
-- s 415: Division 2 "applies to an award of damages against a worker's employer ... if -- (a) the injury was caused by the tort
-- of the employer; and (b) compensation for the injury has been paid or is payable".
-- s 416: Division 2 "does not apply to -- (a) an award of damages in respect of an injury that results in the death of the worker;
-- or (b) an award of damages to which the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies; ... (d) an award of damages
-- against a person who is a worker's employer (a deemed employer) only because of section 215 or 225".
-- s 434(1): "When a third party is liable to pay damages in respect of an injury for which compensation is payable, the worker may
-- take proceedings both against the third party to recover damages and against any person liable to pay compensation"; s 434(2):
-- not "both damages and compensation" -- damages recovered are brought to account.
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `his employer`
    `a person deemed his employer only because of s 215`
    `a third party`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `compensation paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury results in death` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 7 Division 2 constrains the damages` IF
        `the defendant` EQUALS `his employer`
    AND `compensation paid or payable`
    AND (NOT `the injury results in death`)
    AND (NOT `the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies`)

-- s 421(1): proceedings against the employer "must not be commenced" unless "(a) the worker's degree of permanent whole of person
-- impairment resulting from the injury has been assessed to be at least 15% and that assessment has been recorded by the Director
-- as the supporting assessment for the worker's election ...; (b) the worker has elected ... to retain the right to seek the damages
-- and the Director has -- (i) registered the election ...; and (ii) notified the worker in writing". s 422(2): a worker with a
-- terminal disease (s 422(1)) may commence first. s 421(4)(b): no award unless "the court is satisfied that the worker's degree of
-- permanent whole of person impairment resulting from the injury is at least 15%"; s 421(5): the court "is not bound by the
-- supporting assessment".
GIVEN `Division 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `assessed whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER, `election registered and notified` IS A BOOLEAN, `a terminal disease under s 422` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 421 bars commencing proceedings` IF
        `Division 2 applies`
    AND (NOT `a terminal disease under s 422`)
    AND (    `assessed whole person impairment` LESS THAN 15
         OR  (NOT `election registered and notified`))

GIVEN `Division 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole person impairment found by the court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 421 bars an award of damages` IF
        `Division 2 applies`
    AND `whole person impairment found by the court` LESS THAN 15

-- s 424(2): "Unless the court is satisfied that the worker's degree of permanent whole of person impairment is at least 25%", the
-- maximum award against the employer is the prescribed "maximum damages amount for less than 25% impairment" (an INPUT), awarded
-- "only in a most extreme case"; s 424(5): no maximum at 25% or more.
GIVEN `Division 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole person impairment found by the court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damages are capped at the prescribed maximum` IF
        `Division 2 applies`
    AND `whole person impairment found by the court` LESS THAN 25

§§ `423 -- the price of an election under 25%`

-- s 423(1): once the election is registered and the whole person impairment "as assessed by an approved permanent impairment
-- assessor is less than 25%": income compensation for "the first 6 months after the day on which the election is registered" is
-- reduced; none "for any time that is more than 6 months after the registration day"; no permanent impairment compensation; and no
-- medical, miscellaneous or rehabilitation expenses compensation "for expenses incurred after the registration day".
-- s 423(2): the reduced amount is "70%" for "the first 3 months after the registration day" and "50%" for "any other time during
-- the first 6 months". Months are counted here as whole months completed since the registration day.
GIVEN `assessed whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER, `whole months since the registration day` IS A NUMBER, `unreduced amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`income compensation after the election` MEANS
    IF `assessed whole person impairment` AT LEAST 25
    THEN `unreduced amount`
    ELSE IF `whole months since the registration day` LESS THAN 3
         THEN `unreduced amount` TIMES 70 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE IF `whole months since the registration day` LESS THAN 6
              THEN `unreduced amount` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100
              ELSE 0

GIVEN `assessed whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an election ends medical and health expenses compensation for later expenses` IF
    `assessed whole person impairment` LESS THAN 25
